@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch feat/353-provenance-check-workflow); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:529 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "docs: CLAUDE.md provenance-check step before implementation + measurable PR trace (#353)" ;
    bl:number 529 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:353 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr529 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:353 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-16T10:18:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr529Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:abstractText "Added CLAUDE.md step 2b (check provenance before implementing) with a required, greppable PR trace section, and fixed run.sh's parameterization to make it work." ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #353 (fourth slice of the provenance-query-workflow plan, depending on #355's backlog backfill landing) asked for a new CLAUDE.md step, inserted before step 3's sub-agent delegation, telling an agent to check provenance/queries/related_to_file.sparql or related_to_crate.sparql for prior reasoning before starting work. Dag's own follow-up comment on the issue (carried over from a duplicate, #482, he filed independently) sharpened the scope: the check should not be a silent 'read it and proceed' nudge, since he wants to later measure whether it actually makes agents more efficient/grounded — that requires a visible, auditable trace of what happened, not just prose that could be phrased differently every PR. Before writing the step, verified the plan doc's proposed invocation syntax (`run.sh related_to_file.sparql -- <path>`) by actually running it — it does not work: run.sh only ever accepted a single positional arg (the bare query name), and both related_to_file.sparql/related_to_crate.sparql are parameterized via a hardcoded VALUES line inside the .sparql file itself, not via CLI args. Documenting the broken syntax in CLAUDE.md would have shipped a step an agent trusts and immediately hits an error on. Fixed run.sh instead of writing around it with a documented sed/mktemp dance, on the reasoning that a fragile multi-step workaround is exactly the kind of friction that gets skipped under time pressure, which would poison the very measurement this issue exists to enable. The fix substitutes the caller's replacement value into the VALUES line's braces via awk (chosen over sed to avoid delimiter/escaping issues with file paths and prefixed IRIs) into a throwaway mktemp copy, leaving the checked-in .sparql files untouched, and is backward compatible (the original single-arg form still works). Also added .github/pull_request_template.md, since none existed, so the required '## Prior provenance checked' section is prefilled by default rather than depending on an agent remembering a prose convention from CLAUDE.md alone. This PR's own description dogfoods the new step: it queried related_to_file for CLAUDE.md and found PR #344 genuinely relevant (the prior PR that established the 'step 6b'-style sub-lettered-step and self-authored-summary conventions this PR's new 'step 2b' deliberately mirrors), so its trace line reads 'applied — #344' rather than 'none-relevant'." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:529 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr529Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr529 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr529Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Made the provenance-check outcome a required, fixed-format PR-description section ('## Prior provenance checked' with one of exactly three token lines: `provenance-checked: applied — #<PR>`, `none-relevant`, or `skipped — <reason>`, plus a `queried:` line recording what was actually looked up) rather than optional free-form prose." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered leaving the trace as a suggested-but-optional prose note ('mention if you found something relevant'). Rejected because Dag's stated goal is to later measure whether the provenance-check step actually helps agents be more efficient/grounded — optional free-form prose is not comparable or greppable across PRs, can't distinguish 'checked, found nothing' from 'forgot to check', and under time pressure tends to be silently dropped, which would make the eventual measurement impossible rather than just noisy. A fixed small set of token outcomes, including an explicit 'skipped' value (not just silence), keeps every PR's provenance-check outcome auditable and comparable, at the cost of a small amount of extra required boilerplate per PR." .
